cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this software or its results, please cite it as below."
title: "ArithScope: exact arithmetic position channels for Transformer attention"
abstract: >-
  A zero-initialized, Ramanujan-sum relative-position bias for attention heads, with proofs
  (optimal positive-definite periodic comb, CRT composition, alias partitions, residue-blindness
  of incommensurate frequency banks such as RoPE), an exact low-rank form for fused attention
  kernels, and preregistered matched-baseline experiments on length extrapolation.
type: software
authors:
  - family-names: "Hayami"
    given-names: "A."
version: "0.2.0"
license: MIT
date-released: "2026-10-15"
repository-code: "https://github.com/Akari-H-111/ArithScope"
keywords:
  - transformer
  - attention
  - positional encoding
  - length generalization
  - Ramanujan sums
